erenced by an NPC  and is even recognized by stable masters  meaning it has a canon influence on the  world of breath of the wild well since  it's a Canon being that actually exists  in breath of wild lore that means we  have to take what we know about it in  game seriously like the fact that it's  in game description details that legends  say it used to be a sage who died on the  lands that now protects a  now any fan of the Zelda franchise worth  their salt knows that Zelda and sages go  hand in hand the seven sages from  ocarina of time the two sages from Wind  Waker seven sages from a Link to the  Past and six from Twilight Princess at  cetera at Sega and Zelda games tend to  take their sages very seriously so  firstly in order to speculate on what  the Lord of the mountains backstory  might be let's first define what exactly  a Zelda game means by sage according to  real world classical philosophy a sage  is a person who has obtained a lot of  wisdom they're even called wise men in a  Link to the Past but their real purposes  differ from game to game  sometimes they're useful in sealing away  Ganon and sometimes they're useful in  restoring power to the master sword and  other times they try to stab Ganondorf  in the gut but each time they make an  appearance they represent an element and  are normally a member of a race of  people who complement said element but  this isn't always the case as in a Link  to the Past in Twilight Princess they're  all of the same race of just featureless  people so in summary a sage in zelda  lore is simply an individual who was  normally a part of a group that served  some divine purpose for the goddesses  yep that's basically it so now back to  the lord of the mountain Satori was a  sage that much is known from its in-game  description it's also stated that it  died on the land it now protects and I'd  wager it's pretty safe to assume this  land that it died on is the Satori  Mountain what would the name and it  being the only 